  "details": "So this bug appears in desktop mode and it might be in VR as well but you can move around in VR so it's really only a desktop issue, you see the issue is that whenever a desktop user enters a portal accept an invite or goes home there camera is supposed to snap back up in Center however the bug has a 75% to 99% chance of not snapping back up to Center the camera and just locking the camera outside of the Go Button, I had informed this to a friend and a friend of theirs said why don't you just enable the skip Go Button cuz that I said because if you are getting portal trolled or if a hacker teleport you to a portal in which the world will crash your game / computer you have the ability to not enter that world thus not crashing, to avoid crashers teleporting you to a portal and sending you to a crashing world or avoid getting portal trolled you have the option to just stay in the loading screen and go back home, this bug locks your camera in the angle of which you are entering a portal or accepting an invite or going home and it will lock you in that angle.\n\nI have tested this with multiple avatars both small and tall and in between and it still happens, even tested portals going to my World's and Portals going to other peoples worlds even the official worlds and it still happens not all the time but a lot of the time it will happen say 75+% , as far as I can tell the camera is just not snapping back up and centering itself when desktop uses enter the loading screen, however the bug can vary between people but when I do it it's a 90% chance of it happening to me , and that could be very problematic for me because I test world's to see if they're optimized or if they are even working, if I can't go to the world then that can lead to some issues and delaying projects, \n\nI made a short video showing how and what happens due to this bug, https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=do8S8D1jolM\n\nso the recap the bug does not snap the camera back to its Center angle when entering the loading screen regardless of Avatar and regardless of portals and regardless of how you are entering the loading screen while in desktop",
